prompt:
A complete 30-second narrative segment, 16:9, sculpted Chinese 3D animated feature style. Woven cloth, dimensional faces, cohesive sculpted hair, restrained wood and bronze. Natural Mandarin dialogue with lip synchronization, footsteps, water and cloth sounds. Each timeline interval is an action beat. Camera cuts follow the CAMERA PLAN; continuous takes carry successive beats through one moving camera. Begin by matching the opening composition in @Image1. Reference portraits define identity and clothing; the current action defines pose and placement. Technical diagrams define mechanical connections translated into the scene materials. Paper surfaces stay suitable for later Chinese typography.
REFERENCE ROLES:
@Image1: opening intact copper plug, right bandaged palm and awl point.
@Image2: Lu Zhao begins in dry teal clothes, intact left shoulder, bandaged RIGHT palm.
@Image3: Lu Zhao with anatomical LEFT shoulder cut and RIGHT palm bandage, applies after the knife cut.
@Image4: Ge Ya 葛牙 brown hood and short hair identity.
@Image5: Ali 阿砾 blue clothing.
@Image6: Wen Xi 闻溪 mint clothing.
@Image7: water-trough owner 水槽货主 in beige and green apron.
@Image8: house door LEFT, net rack RIGHT, stone gutter lower right.
@Image9: wood rail and upper-tied net with loose heavy lower corner.
@Image10: Ge Ya short knife.
@Image11: one ordinary short black awl with old hemp-wrapped grip.
@Image12: detached brown hood after the final body pin.
@Image13: intact lunch bowl on low door stand.
@Image14: small purse and tied strings of copper coins.
CAMERA PLAN: At 0s show the copper plug hand detail. At 2s sound-bridge the water into a payment cut. At 4s cut to the spatial wide view with the house door on the left and net rack on the right. From 4s to 30s the entire confrontation is one uninterrupted tracking take on the same side of the door-to-net axis. Move sideways for the hostage handover, follow Lu Zhao backward toward the door and then rightward toward the rack. Lower continuously for the mesh catching the knife and maintain a three-quarter side angle that reveals both hands: drive the awl through folded mesh and rail, release the planted awl, press Ge Ya RIGHT elbow with Lu Zhao LEFT palm, bend Ge Ya RIGHT wrist, take the knife, push it inward to slacken mesh, slide it clear and drop it into the lower-right gutter. Maintain visible continuity through Ge Ya left punch and Lu Zhao right hand catching that left wrist. Arc gently on the same side of the axis. End with Lu Zhao uninjured right shoulder pinning Ge Ya to the post, both wrists controlled and the detached hood on the ground.
TIMELINE:
[0–2s] Next-day caption. Lu Zhao's bandaged hand already holds the original awl against the copper plug. Then one straight push opens it and clear water falls into the bucket; the awl withdraws along its entry path as the water sound bridges to the next shot.
[2–4s] Cut to payment time: the original awl is already sheathed at Lu Zhao's belt as the trough owner places sixty copper coins in his hand. Then he pockets the coins and reaches toward lunch on the low stand; Wen Xi stops outside and looks past his shoulder.
[2.1–3.3s] 水槽货主, visible speaker with synchronized lips, says exactly in Mandarin: “六十铜。”
[4–8s] Ge Ya at screen right twists Ali's right arm and holds a short knife against his ribs. Lu Zhao and his sister's door remain at screen left. Then Ge Ya shoves Ali half a step forward and calls Lu Zhao, while Wen Xi moves within reach to receive Ali.
[4.3–6.5s] 葛牙, visible speaker with synchronized lips, says exactly in Mandarin: “照子，跟我走。”
[8–10s] Lu Zhao sets the lunch bowl firmly on the low stand by the door. Then he takes two steps toward Ge Ya with his hands away from the sheathed awl and stops where Wen Xi can receive Ali.
[8.2–9.5s] 陆照, visible speaker with synchronized lips, says exactly in Mandarin: “先放他。”
[10–13.5s] Ge Ya releases Ali into Wen Xi's arms. Then before Lu Zhao can draw, Ge Ya's knife cuts the cloth at Lu Zhao's left shoulder; Lu Zhao recoils half a step and draws the awl with his right hand as blood spreads at the left shoulder.
[13.5–16.5s] Lu Zhao's retreat puts his sister's door just behind his left shoulder, with crockery audible inside. Then he changes direction and moves right toward the drying net frame, drawing Ge Ya after him as the camera tracks; Wen Xi and Ali remain safely by the left-hand door.
[16.5–18.5s] The net curtain is tied along the top rail and hangs in a loose wet heap beside Lu Zhao's foot. Then he kicks its loose lower corner over Ge Ya's pursuing knife; the wet mesh wraps the blade while Lu Zhao steps beside the net with his awl.
[18.5–20s] Close detail shows mesh wrapped around the knife spine while Ge Ya grips the handle outside. Then he saws through two strands but the remaining wet net stays wrapped; the folded corner reaches the near wooden rail as Lu Zhao's awl enters frame.
[20–23s] A side view includes Lu Zhao's two-handed grip, the folded net corner and the wooden rail, with his injured left shoulder visible. Then he drives the awl straight through the folded mesh into and through the rail so the handle traps the corner; Ge Ya's pulling knife draws his wrist toward the now-taut net. Lu Zhao releases the awl, leaving it fixed in the rail.
[23–27s] Ge Ya still grips the knife in his right hand with the net taut. Lu Zhao braces Ge Ya right elbow against the rail with Lu Zhao left palm and bends the knife wrist back with his right hand. Then Ge Ya opens his fingers in pain; Lu Zhao visibly takes the handle, pushes it slightly into the net to slacken the mesh and slides the blade out along its spine. Once the blade clears the mesh he releases it into the established lower-right gutter beside his foot, keeping the elbow pinned with his left palm.
[27–30s] Lu Zhao's left palm pins Ge Ya's right elbow against the rail; his right hand has just released the knife into the gutter. Then Ge Ya's left fist hits Lu Zhao beside the ear. As the fist retracts, Lu Zhao catches that left wrist with his right hand, folds it across Ge Ya's chest and turns his body and uninjured right shoulder to wedge Ge Ya against the post, controlling both arms. Ge Ya's hood catches the rail and falls.
RIGHT palm is bandaged throughout. LEFT shoulder cloth begins intact, gets cut during 10–13.5s and retains that small wound afterward. The uninjured RIGHT shoulder performs the final body pin. Awl sheath is palm-sized at waist.
The original awl stays a single small hemp-handled tool. All characters preserve their reference identities across camera movements. End at the last specified action state at 30 seconds.
